message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Anatomical metastasis graphs with edge-wise desmoplastic conductances: lumped burden and edge-rate identifiability"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  When each organ-graph edge carries an explicit desmoplastic conductance, do
  metastatic edge rates remain unidentified from lumped systemic burden, or do
  barrier observables restore an identifiable subset? On a four-node toy, a
  series flux collapses each shedding rate and conductance into one
  combination. Lumped burden leaves that joint parameter at practical rank 2
  of 6, with a three-dimensional structural kernel along the series level
  set. Site-resolved node burdens, which identify the three fluxes when each
  edge has a single rate, still reach only rank 3 of 6 once the conductance
  is free. Barrier readings restore a subset: all six parameters when the
  nodes and the three stalled fractions are both recorded, and a proper
  subset under thinner schedules. A hold-up generator is full structural rank
  under the lump and practical rank 3 of 6. Not a medical device. No dose.
  No cure.
